From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:15:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: tps65132: Retry the first read before registering

The OCP2131 panel bias on the Zinwa Q25 does not acknowledge the first
transfer on its bus after boot. Registration then fails on reading the
current voltage, with -ENXIO, and the driver core does not retry, so the
panel and the display pipeline wait for the supply forever. Every later
transfer succeeds, including a manual rebind seconds after boot.

Read VPOS up to three times before registering, and defer if the chip
still does not answer.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/regulator/tps65132-regulator.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/tps65132-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/tps65132-regulator.c
index 9c2f0dd4..019fd98e 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/tps65132-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/tps65132-regulator.c
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@ static int tps65132_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	struct regulator_dev *rdev;
 	struct regmap *rmap;
 	struct regulator_config config = { };
-	int id;
+	unsigned int val;
+	int id, tries;
 	int ret;
 
 	tps = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*tps), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -241,6 +242,18 @@ static int tps65132_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* Some parts NAK the first transfer after power-up; retry it here. */
+	for (tries = 0; tries < 3; tries++) {
+		ret = regmap_read(rmap, TPS65132_REG_VPOS, &val);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER, "no response: %d\n", ret);
+	if (tries)
+		dev_info(dev, "responded after %d failed read(s)\n", tries);
+
 	i2c_set_clientdata(client, tps);
 	tps->dev = dev;
 
-- 
2.55.0

